docs/mcp-code-mode-rationale.md:68:Local managed artifacts are generated under one exclusively owned server artifact directory with safe names, per-file and aggregate limits, persisted TTL cleanup, MIME type, byte count, and SHA-256 integrity metadata; they are not arbitrary user-chosen file writes. A second live owner fails closed instead of racing a stale manifest. Hosted `render_png` returns base64 or an image content block only.
docs/design/system/pr449-current-measurements-2026-10-23.md:70:Zero of six required OFF tails reaches the declared improvement with both local A/A pairs healthy. Several aggregate A/A controls also fail: OFF whole75 baseline/ELK A/A are 1.034882/1.049472, and NORMAL ELK A/A is 1.174702. These observations do not establish a causal speedup or slowdown. The mandatory wrapper rejects the candidate; favorable NORMAL whole/DAG ratios cannot override the failed H27, per-input, A/A and tail gates. No memory, delivery or broad-quality promotion run follows this failed timing result. Two measured calls per input per round and three fresh rounds provide limited precision; the experiment establishes no p95 or throughput guarantee.
docs/design/system/pr449-current-measurements-2026-10-23.md:84:All 14 per-input guards, 485 independent bindings, public payload comparisons and deadlines pass; the aggregate targets still fail. OFF A/A also exceeds its reciprocal 1.05 limit. The measured first-render window includes full SVG and receipt UTF8 consumption; bootstrap is outside the CPU windows. Separate import/render and wall-time decompositions are descriptive and cannot replace the combined CPU target. This experiment uses historical sources `e039bc9a` → `3f8c2df5`, not current968/ec72. It establishes no current runtime, warm throughput or memory improvement. The candidate's earlier 574,173-byte Architecture payload also still exceeds 574,000. No retry or promotion follows.
