docs/design/system/pr449-frontier-2026-10-23.md:28:Lower values are preferred for the numerical aesthetics and resource metrics below. “Off” and “normal” mean the declared cache policies. Memory ratios are native/ELK medians of three same-round ratios; they are not ratios of separately computed medians or sums of per-input medians.
docs/design/system/pr449-frontier-2026-10-23.md:104:Original five-pass timing failures remain failed. A separate one-prewarm/two-pass SVG protocol `@2` is implemented prospectively and under independent review, but is not yet finally frozen, declared or executed. It retains all 75 inputs: 75 prewarm calls plus 150 timed calls per worker, 225 total; two samples per input per round limit precision. It must be explicitly declared before any new candidate product cost, retain all 75 inputs and numerical targets, and cannot be used to retry the rejected zero or phase candidates. The original UTF8 target contract remains unmet; no timing worker has qualified its product benefit. The workload also changes explicitly: `@1` materializes receipt JSON inside its metric window but creates the UTF8 receipt buffer outside; `@2` must include both full JSON and UTF8 materialization inside. Neither method can be relabelled as the other.
