docs/design/system/layout-exploration/layout-literature.md:61:**Experiment D:** count ranks, helper vertices, arcs, route-grid vertices, candidate builds, full geometry conversions, and certification passes per input, and join those counts to allocation profiles. If expansion correlates with the six cyclic allocation regressions, prototype sparse long-edge chains behind an internal flag. If route states dominate, test the one-bend visibility representation instead. If repeated reconstruction dominates, reuse immutable topology/measured dimensions and candidate-local scratch arrays with explicit ownership. Preserve all label ranks, original arrows, duplicate-edge identity and proof inputs. Reject changed work caps, disappearing declines, stale scratch state on edits, unbounded caches, or a faster warm result with worse uncached behavior. Target both uncached outliers below 1.5 times ELK and all six allocation regressions reduced, without sacrificing the quality gates. Run fresh A/A controls; do not divide noisy timings by A/A as a correction.
